      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand during a period of 30 minutes, we need to calculate the circumference of the circle traced by the tip of the second hand and then multiply it by the number of revolutions the second hand makes in 30 minutes.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the circumference of the circle traced by the tip of the second hand. The radius of the circle is given as 6 cm. The formula for the circumference \\(C\\) of a circle is:\n\n\\[ C = 2 \\pi r \\]\n\nSubstituting the given radius:\n\n\\[ C = 2 \\pi \\times 6 = 12 \\pi \\text{ cm} \\]\n\nThis is the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand in one complete revolution. Now, we need to determine how many revolutions the second hand makes in 30 minutes. The second hand completes one revolution every 60 seconds (1 minute). Therefore, in 30 minutes, the second hand will complete:\n\n\\[ \\text{Number of revolutions} = \\frac{30 \\text{ minutes}}{1 \\text{ minute/revolution}} = 30 \\text{ revolutions} \\]\n\nTo find the total distance traveled by the tip of the second hand in 30 minutes, we multiply the circumference of the circle by the number of revolutions:\n\n\\[ \\text{Total distance} = 30 \\times 12 \\pi = 360 \\pi \\text{ cm} \\]\n\nThus, the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand during a period of 30 minutes is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{360\\pi} \\]",
