    "text": "To determine how far the tip of the second hand travels during a period of 30 minutes, we need to calculate the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand in one minute and then multiply that by 30.\n\nFirst, let's find the circumference of the circle traced by the tip of the second hand. The second hand is 6 cm long, so the radius of the circle is 6 cm. The formula for the circumference \\(C\\) of a circle is given by:\n\n\\[\nC = 2 \\pi r\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the radius \\(r = 6\\) cm, we get:\n\n\\[\nC = 2 \\pi \\times 6 = 12 \\pi \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nThis means that the tip of the second hand travels \\(12 \\pi\\) cm in one complete revolution around the circle. Since a minute is one complete revolution of the second hand, the tip of the second hand travels \\(12 \\pi\\) cm in one minute.\n\nTo find out how far the tip of the second hand travels in 30 minutes, we multiply the distance traveled in one minute by 30:\n\n\\[\n12 \\pi \\times 30 = 360 \\pi \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand during a period of 30 minutes is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{360\\pi}\n\\]",
